"MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/hgraph/nodes/f2e594d1b5e6.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/hgraph/nodes/f3e941ede3d7.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/hgraph/nodes/f7c9dc03eee5.md", "category": "other", "add": 8, "del": 1}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/hgraph/nodes/f89dc48900f4.md", "category": "other", "add": 1, "del": 1}], "lean": {"files": 3, "add": 296, "del": 7, "loc_after": 3894, "loc_code_after": 2690, "loc_delta": 289, "loc_code_delta": 103, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {"theorem": 19, "def": 24, "lemma": 72, "instance": 3}, "decl_delta": {"def": 2, "theorem": 8}}, "blueprint": {"files": 0, "add": 0, "del": 0, "loc_after": 0, "loc_code_after": 0, "loc_delta": 0, "loc_code_delta": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_after": {}, "decl_delta": {}}, "sorry_delta": 0, "other_count": 60}, {"sha": "31e01a7699a39c0485e1dc2360123d498adb8e94", "short_sha": "31e01a7699", "subject": "h1(O_P1) = 0 and genus P1 = 0: the genus-0 UniformVanishing producer now HAS a witness", "summary": "**The brick.** `LaurentChartData.subsingleton_h1Cok`: the Cech cokernel of $\\mathcal{O}$ on the two-chart cover vanishes, for ANY `Spec k`-scheme carrying Laurent chart data -- no properness, smoothness, irreducibility or cohomological finiteness; the signature binds only the datum. At the concrete datum this gives `subsingleton_hModule_one_p1Over` and `genus_p1Over_eq_zero`, every field. `Subsingleton` first and `finrank` as corollary, since a genus computation alone cannot give vanishing.\n\n**What it unblocks.** `Ledger/VanishingFieldDescent.lean` (r7) produced `UniformVanishing C` from `Subsingleton H^1(O_C)` and recorded in its own NON-VACUITY section that AJC discharged that hypothesis at NO curve -- a true implication with no instance (I-0746). `uniformVanishing_p1Over` discharges it: extension-uniform bounded vanishing WITNESSED at a curve AJC has, threshold $d + g = 0$, serving every extension simultaneously.\n\n**I-0746 mis-priced the obstacle, and that is the reusable finding.** It measured the blocker as structural -- `LaurentChartData` has `span_pow_x` per chart but no field for integer powers on the OVERLAP -- and prescribed either a new field (\"breaks every constructor in the project\") or a span-of-localization lemma. Neither was needed: `span_ladder_overlap` derives it from three lemmas already in the same file, and `exists_pow_mul_eq_res` IS the basic-open localization the prescription asked someone to build. A one-screen derivation had been priced as a deferred epic.\n\n**Five stale status claims corrected in four sibling files**, because the landing makes them wrong in the other direction. `ExtensionUniformity` said \"genus 0 is now closed\" of a state where the producer had no witness -- too strong then, true now, rewritten to say which file supplies which half. The four surviving copies of \"AJC exhibits no curve satisfying its hypothesis\" in `VanishingFieldDescent` are past-tensed (r7's own lesson: fixing one copy and leaving another is worse than fixing none), plus the pointers in `GenusFieldInvariance` and `SectionsFieldBaseChange`.\n\n**Scope, three cluster-P items kept apart.** Single-field vanishing: closed where a Laurent datum exists, i.e. at $\\mathbb{P}^1$; genus $\\ge 1$ has no datum. Extension-uniformity: now non-vacuous as a type, still open in general with r7's residue unchanged (`UniformBaseDivisor C d`, $d>0$, needing a divisor-level base-change comparison AJC lacks). Global generation: untouched by this file.\n\n**Provenance and checks.** Rederived in AJC's abstractions; porting was not an option and this is measured, not assumed -- AJCR has ZERO occurrences of `LaurentChartData` and no `genus = 0` theorem. `lake build AlgebraicJacobian.RiemannRoch.Ledger.P1Vanishing` 8726 jobs EXIT=0, module 0 sorries; the three `sorry` warnings in the log are pre-existing in `Picard/`.\n\n**Note on provenance of the file's first appearance.** `P1Vanishing.lean` was swept into HEAD by run 0075's `system: baseline` commit before this commit could land -- the I-0693 hazard, a message that describes none of the mathematics. This commit carries the actual content and the docstring corrections.", "created_at": "2026-07-29T13:42:29+08:00", "role": "horizon", "kind": "agent", "files": [{"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Ledger/ExtensionUniformity.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 20, "del": 8, "loc_before": 435, "loc_after": 447, "loc_code_before": 111, "loc_code_after": 111, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"instance": 1, "theorem": 6, "def": 2}, "decl_after": {"instance": 1, "theorem": 6, "def": 2}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Ledger/GenusFieldInvariance.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 4, "del": 2, "loc_before": 476, "loc_after": 478, "loc_code_before": 188, "loc_code_after": 188, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"lemma": 2, "def": 4, "abbrev": 1, "theorem": 9}, "decl_after": {"lemma": 2, "def": 4, "abbrev": 1, "theorem": 9}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Ledger/P1Vanishing.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 20, "del": 2, "loc_before": 332, "loc_after": 350, "loc_code_before": 132, "loc_code_after": 132, "sorry_before": 0, "sorry_after": 0, "sorry_delta": 0, "decl_before": {"theorem": 8, "def": 1}, "decl_after": {"theorem": 8, "def": 1}, "decl_delta": {}, "added": false, "deleted": false}, {"path": "MainProjects/Algebraic-Jacobian-Challenge/AlgebraicJacobian/RiemannRoch/Ledger/SectionsFieldBaseChange.lean", "category": "lean", "add": 2, "del": 1, "loc_before": 402, "loc_a